  "body": "Follow-up of #1091. The fix there re-reads a vertical dive convicted against the stock's flat top (`stock_top_z`) against the stock and part solids under the tool stack (`verify::acquit_by_stock_top`). Lateral rapids are not re-read: a link or traverse below the clearance plane that crosses a low part of a stepped \"from model\" or carried stock, above the stock really under it, is still convicted as if the stock's highest point stood there (`rapids.rs`, `Rest::surface_before`'s cap).\n\nIt refuses, it does not gouge, so P2.\n\nDone means: a lateral rapid over the low step of a stepped stock, above it by more than the tolerance, is not convicted; the same rapid crossing the boss (or with the boss under the tool's rim or stack along the way) still is; pinned in `sim::verify::stock_top` or a sibling, the existing rapid-law pins unchanged.\n",
